+# Deploying the Static IPFS Site
+
+This project is configured for a static Next.js export when `NEXT_PUBLIC_IPFS_BUILD=true`. Do not upload stale output: always clean `.next` and `out` first.
+
+## 1. Deploy the Contract to Base
+
+Use a real deployer keystore with enough ETH on Base:
+
+```bash
+yarn deploy --network base --keystore <your-keystore-name>
+```
+
+This writes the Base deployment ABI/address into `packages/nextjs/contracts/deployedContracts.ts`.
+
+## 2. Build for IPFS
+
+Replace the production URL with the gateway or ENS name the site will use:
+
+```bash
+cd packages/nextjs
+rm -rf .next out
+
+NEXT_PUBLIC_TARGET_NETWORK=base \
+NEXT_PUBLIC_PRODUCTION_URL="https://<your-name>.eth.link" \
+NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_RPC_URL="https://<your-base-rpc-url>" \
+NODE_OPTIONS="--require ./polyfill-localstorage.cjs" \
+NEXT_PUBLIC_IPFS_BUILD=true \
+NEXT_PUBLIC_IGNORE_BUILD_ERROR=true \
+yarn build
+```
+
+## 3. Verify the Static Output Before Upload
+
+```bash
+test -f out/index.html
+ls out/*/index.html
+grep -R "Tip Jar" out | head
+grep "og:image" out/index.html
+stat -f "%Sm" app/page.tsx
+stat -f "%Sm" out
+```
+
+The `out` timestamp must be newer than the source timestamp. The generated route files should be directories with `index.html` files because IPFS needs trailing slashes.
+
+## 4. Upload to IPFS
+
+No upload has been run for this deliverable. When ready:
+
+```bash
+yarn bgipfs upload config init -u https://upload.bgipfs.com
+yarn bgipfs upload out
+```
+
+Save the returned CID.
+
+## 5. Verify After Upload
+
+Replace `<CID>` below:
+
+```bash
+CID=<CID>
+GATEWAY=https://community.bgipfs.com/ipfs/$CID
+
+curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}\n" -L "$GATEWAY/"
+curl -s -L "$GATEWAY/" | grep "Tip Jar"
+curl -s -L "$GATEWAY/" | grep "og:image"
+```
+
+If you use ENS, set the content hash to `ipfs://<CID>`, then verify:
+
+```bash
+NAME=<your-name>.eth
+RESOLVER=$(cast call 0x00000000000C2e074eC69A0dFb2997BA6C7d2e1e "resolver(bytes32)(address)" $(cast namehash $NAME) --rpc-url https://eth.llamarpc.com)
+cast call $RESOLVER "contenthash(bytes32)(bytes)" $(cast namehash $NAME) --rpc-url https://eth.llamarpc.com
+curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}\n" -L "https://$NAME.link"
+```
